  "body": "One scenario that might deserve an entry in the [use cases document](use-cases.bs):\r\n\r\nThere are three \"dockless\" bike share services in Seattle which allow anyone with a smartphone to rent a bike for 30 minutes or an hour.  This is currently done using a native app that works as follows:\r\n\r\n1. App downloads a map of available bikes nearby\r\n1. User finds a bike, scans a QR code on the bike to get an unlock password from the cloud.\r\n1. App uses BTLE to send an unlock request to the electronic bike lock.\r\n1. A successful unlock is reported back via BTLE and the bike is reported unlocked to the app, which starts the rental.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, I believe locking the bike signals the app via BTLE that the rental has ended.\r\n\r\nWith Web Bluetooth (and other Web APIs), this could be done using a Web app.",
